<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<class name="Controller" inherits="Node" api_type="extension" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/godotengine/godot/master/doc/class.xsd">
	<brief_description>
		Base class for anything that can possess a [Pawn].
	</brief_description>
	<description>
		Holds the possession relationship. See [PlayerController] for the player-facing subclass.
		Controllers add themselves to [method World.get_controllers] from [code]_enter_tree[/code] and take themselves out again in [code]_exit_tree[/code], so the world list also picks up AI controllers and controllers a designer placed in a level by hand, and can never hold a freed one.
		[b]A subclass that overrides [code]_enter_tree[/code] or [code]_exit_tree[/code] must call the base implementation[/b], or it will never be registered - Godot binds only the most derived override.
	</description>
